ive-star defensive end D.J. Jacobs, the No. 2 overall recruit in the 2027 class, committed to Miami on Thursday hours after pulling his commitment from Ohio State.","published":"2026-11-26T22:58:35.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50606746/top-de-recruit-dj-jacobs-commits-miami-hours-decommitting-ohio-state","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"D.J. Jacobs decommits from Ohio State, sources say, making top DE available again","description":"D.J. Jacobs, the No. 2 overall recruit in the 2027 class, has decommitted from Ohio State, sources told ESPN, with Tennessee, Georgia and Miami among the leading contenders for the five-star defensive end.","published":"2026-11-26T21:21:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50606035/sources-de-dj-jacobs-decommits-ohio-state","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Friday Night Lights,' 'Ted Lasso' top poll ranking 21st-century sports shows","description":"A Seton Hall poll crowns America's favorite modern fictional sports TV series.﻿","published":"2026-11-26T16:01:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/story/_/id/50576889/top-fictional-sports-series-21st-century","type":"Story","byline":"Brianna Williams","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"The oldest grudge in football","description":"When Texas Tech and its brash benefactor bought their way into the college football big time, they were settling an old West Texas score.","published":"2026-11-26T13:12:44.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50427039/texas-tech-puf-cody-campbell","type":"Story","byline":"Dave Wilson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Take a 360-degree look at college football's iconic rivalry trophies","description":"Whether ancient, animal or absurd, college football's rivalry trophies take many shapes.","published":"2026-11-26T13:09:54.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/feature/story/_/id/50371090/college-football-rivalry-trophies","type":"Eticket","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"USC band won't perform at UCLA football game after members vandalized campus","description":"The USC Trojan Marching Band will not perform during Saturday's rivalry game against UCLA after members of the band vandalized a portion of UCLA's campus.","published":"2026-11-26T14:39:43.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50600615/usc-band-perform-members-vandalized-ucla-campus","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Paolo Uggetti","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Kent State TD overturned by replay was incorrect decision, MAC says","description":"A Kent State touchdown catch should not have been overturned by replay to incomplete at the end of Tuesday's 17-12 loss to Eastern Michigan, the Mid-American Conference said Wednesday.","published":"2026-11-25T23:05:40.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50597875/kent-state-td-overturned-replay-was-incorrect-mac-says","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 College Football Playoff National Championship odds","description":"Odds and futures to win the 2027 College Football Playoff National Championship.","published":"2026-11-25T19:44:57.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/47664633/2027-college-football-playoff-national-championship-odds-futures","type":"Story","byline":"Doug Greenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Chris Creighton out as coach at Eastern Michigan after 13 seasons","description":"Chris Creighton is out as head coach at Eastern Michigan after 13 seasons with the school.","published":"2026-11-25T19:05:05.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50595706/creighton-coach-eastern-michigan-13-seasons","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Judge denies SEC's request for TRO against LSU in Dec. 3 vote","description":"A federal judge denied the SEC's request for a temporary restraining order to keep LSU from interfering with a Dec. 3 vote of presidents and chancellors on whether to remove the school from the conference.","published":"2026-11-25T20:02:54.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-sports/story/_/id/50595702/judge-denies-sec-request-tro-lsu-dec-3-vote","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5081821/kenyatta-jackson-jr","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kenyatta_Jackson"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Kenyatta Jackson","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kenyatta_Jackson","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-22T04:17:47Z","intro":"Kenyatta Jackson Jr. (born February 11, 2004) is an American college football defensive end for the Ohio State Buckeyes.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Jackson attended Chaminade–Madonna College Preparatory School located in Hollywood, Florida. During his senior season, he totaled 55 tackles, 17 tackles for loss, 15 quarter back hurries and 14 sacks, where for his performance he was named the Florida Gatorade Player of the Year. Coming out of high school, Jackson was rated as a four-star recruit, the 7th overall defensive end, and the 78th overall player in the class of 2022, where he committed to play college football for the Ohio State Buckeyes over offers from other schools such as Alabama, Auburn, Clemson, Florida, Florida State, Georgia Tech, Miami, North Carolina, Nebraska, Oklahoma, Oregon, and Penn State."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Heading into his true freshman season in 2022, Jackson lost his black stripe before the start of the season, where he chose to wear the jersey #97, which Ohio State greats like Joey Bosa, Nick Bosa, and Cameron Heyward all wore. In his freshman season in 2022 he recorded just two tackles. During the 2023 season, Jackson notched seven tackles with two being for a loss and a sack and a half. He finished the 2024 season, playing in all 16 games, recording 15 tackles and a sack and a half, as he helped the Buckeyes win the 2025 National Championship."}]}}